# Testing

- A test proves one behaviour a caller can observe: the return value, the thrown error, or the side effect that is part of the contract.
- Name the test for that behaviour, not for the function list it happens to touch.
- Cover the failure path that protects an invariant (a missing required value, a refused unsafe path), not only the happy path.
- Build the smallest input that reaches the behaviour. Do not start a service when a function call will do.
- Keep the test next to the code it covers. A change to the contract updates the test in the same change.

```ts
it("rejects a non-root deploy account named root", () => {
  expect(deployUser("root")).toBe(false);
});
```
